{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Who sees the vision of Shaddai, sees.</b> The verse teaches us that his rank did not reach the rank of the patriarchs, and needless to say the rank of prophecy like Moses; rather, he fell short of it by two rungs, for the prophecy of the patriarchs was in El Shaddai, while his prophecy was in the vision of Shaddai." "<b>And thus</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: מחזה שדי is not שדי, for the patriarchs were באל שדי, but Balaam was במחזה של שדי. Therefore he called himself גלוי עינים — 'with unveiled eyes' — for he is of the rank of the prophets, of whom it is said (II Kings 6): ״פקח נא את עיניו״, and this too is said: ״ויגל ה׳ את עיני בלעם״. And what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted — אבל באומות העולם קם — the intention is not that Balaam's prophecy was equal to the prophecy of Moses, heaven forbid; rather, their intention, of blessed memory, is to say: ולא קם נביא עוד בישראל כמשה אשר ידעו ה׳ — the verse equates Moses to Balaam not in the rank of prophecy but in the matter of knowledge, to say that just as the Holy One, blessed be He, knew Moses face to face and his prophecy was clarified to him like a man speaking with his fellow, so the prophecy came clarified to Balaam for the honor of Israel, in all that he prophesied concerning them for all that was to come upon them. This is the intention of the Rav, of blessed memory, along with some of his language. Or one may say: אבל באומות העולם קם — at the time of blessing, for he needed to prophesy with the attribute of mercy, like Moses, for without it Israel would not have endured; but after the blessing, prophecy departed from him and he returned to his divinations. <br><b>Fallen.</b> As in (Genesis 15): ״ותרדמה נפלה על אברם״. <br><b>And with unveiled eyes.</b> That is, he sees even though he is asleep, in the manner of what is written (Song 5): ״אני ישנה ולבי ער״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:44.736334217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}